  "salt": "fq7Htkx5uHey9BG6v5H7fg==",
  "text": "Deirdre (also Derdriu or Deridriu) was an Irish heroine. People called her \"Deirdre of the Sorrows.\" Her tale is one of the Three Sorrows of Ireland. The other two are the Children of Lir and the Sons of Tuireann. Deirdre was born during a feast. Her father Fedlimid mac Daill held the feast for Concobar mac Nessa, king of Ulster. The druid Cathbad foretold her fate. She would become the most beautiful woman in Ireland, he said. Her beauty would destroy the kingdom. Concobar chose to rear her as his prize. He gave her to Leborcham at Emain Macha. One day Deirdre saw a raven drink the blood of a calf on fresh snow. She wanted a man with hair like the raven, skin like snow, and lips like blood. That man was Noísiu, son of Uisneach and a nephew of the king. Deirdre and Noísiu fled with his brothers Ardán and Ainnle. They crossed to Scotland and lived near Loch Etive. Concobar lured them back to Ireland. On landing, Noísiu and his brothers were killed. Deirdre reproached the king for the deed.",
